### 1. Create an order (expect 201 + Location header)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "productId": 2,
    "quantity": 2
}

### 1b. Check product 1 stock went down by 2 (product-service)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

### 2. Get the order (expect 200, totalPrice = 2 x 15500.00 = 31000.00)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders/1

### 3. Order that does not exist (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders/999

### 4. Product that does not exist (expect 404, translated from product-service)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "productId": 999,
    "quantity": 1
}

### 5. Not enough stock (expect 409 with availableStock)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "productId": 4,
    "quantity": 100
}

### 6. Invalid body (expect 400 with field errors)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "quantity": 0
}

### 7. STOP product-service first, then run this (expect 503)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "productId": 1,
    "quantity": 1
}
